# UI reusability and design-system inheritance

Every view, component, and Compose UI in this app must be **reusable by construction** and **built on top of `:core:designsystem`**. Bespoke, single-use, design-system-bypassing UI is not acceptable in feature modules.

This rule sits next to two siblings:

- **`design-system-enforcement.mdc`** — *what* tokens / `P*` to use (no bespoke styling).
- **`lean-classes-separation.mdc`** — *how big* a file/class can grow before extraction.

This rule covers the **before-you-write** decision: is there already a reusable composable for this, and how do I build mine so the next feature can reuse it?

## Hard rules (always apply)

### 1. Search before you write

Before adding any composable under `features/*/ui/` or `features/*/components/`:

1. **Search `:core:designsystem`** for an existing **`P*`** primitive (`PButton`, `PCard`, `PDetailRow`, `PStatusBadge`, `PEmptyState`, `PRouteSection`, `PModalBottomSheet`, etc.).
2. **Search the feature's `components/`** folder for an existing local composable.
3. **Search sibling features' `components/`** when the surface is cross-role (e.g. shipper/carrier showing the same package data).
4. Only after all three searches come up empty, write a new composable — and write it to be reusable from the start (see rule 3).

A new composable that duplicates an existing `P*` or feature component is grounds to reject the PR.

### 2. Inherit from the design system — never reimplement it

Every new UI must **compose `P*` primitives and `Pasabayan*` tokens**, not reach around them:

| Building a… | Build it from | Never |
|---|---|---|
| Section card with a title and rows | `PCard` + `PDetailRow` + `PasabayanSpacing.*` | hand-rolled `Surface` + `Column` + `.padding(12.dp)` |
| Action footer | `PButton` (primary/secondary/tertiary variants) | Material3 `Button` with custom colors |
| Status indicator | `PStatusBadge` (extend with new status if missing) | hand-rolled `Box` with `.background(Color(0xFF…))` |
| Empty / zero state | `PEmptyState` | bespoke icon + headline + body layout |
| Sheet / modal scaffold | `PDetailSheetScaffold` (see `detail-sheet-scaffold-conformance.mdc`) | hand-rolled title row + close + scroll |
| Loading state | `PCircularProgress` inside the same scaffold/card pattern as siblings | inline `CircularProgressIndicator` with bespoke padding |

**Rule of thumb:** if your new composable's body contains a raw `Color(0xFF…)`, a raw `.dp` literal where a token exists, a Material3 component a `P*` already wraps, or a hand-rolled "card-like" `Surface` + `clip(RoundedCornerShape(...))` — you are reimplementing the design system. Stop and use / extend the primitive.

### 3. Design every new composable to be reused

When you do write a new composable, write it as if a second caller already exists:

- **No private state coupling.** Take inputs as parameters; emit outputs as callbacks (`onClick: () -> Unit`). Do **not** read from a `ViewModel` directly inside a reusable component.
- **No business logic.** Reusable composables format and lay out — they don't fetch, decide, or persist. Logic stays in the ViewModel / use case.
- **Parameter shape is data, not entities.** Prefer small data classes or primitives (`title: String`, `status: PackageStatus`) over passing the whole DTO/domain entity. The component should not know about `PackageDto`.
- **Modifier as the first optional parameter** (`modifier: Modifier = Modifier`), per Compose convention, so callers can size/place it.
- **Slot APIs over flag explosions.** When a component might host varying content, take a `content: @Composable () -> Unit` slot rather than 8 boolean flags.
- **Sensible defaults.** Optional parameters default to the most common case so the simplest call site stays one-line.
- **Previews wrapped in `PasabayanTheme`**, light + dark, with realistic sample data — see `compose-ui-previews.mdc`.

A composable that takes a `ViewModel`, mixes in business logic, or accepts a domain entity is **not reusable** even if it lives in `components/`. Refactor before merging.

### 4. Extract early — share at the right level

| Usage pattern | Where it lives |
|---|---|
| Used in **one screen** only | Inline in the screen file is fine, **until** the block exceeds ~30 lines or becomes its own concept — then extract to `features/<feature>/components/`. |
| Used by **≥ 2 composables in the same feature** | Extract to `features/<feature>/components/`. |
| Used by **≥ 2 features** (e.g. shipper + carrier) | Promote to `:core:designsystem` as a `P*` primitive (or a feature-shared composable in `shared/` only when truly shell-level). |
| Recurring **visual pattern** (card chrome, row layout, badge, empty state) | Promote to `:core:designsystem` and add a token entry in `android-spec/14-design-system.md`. |

**Trigger for promotion:** the second time you'd need to copy-paste a composable across features, **stop and promote it** to `:core:designsystem` in its own PR before consuming it from the feature.

### 5. Cross-role parity — same primitives, same composition

When the same content exists for two roles (shipper vs carrier package detail, sender vs recipient address card), the two views must:

- Use the **same `P*` primitives** in the **same order**.
- Share **section composables** (extracted under the feature's `components/` or `:core:designsystem`).
- Differ **only** in actions (buttons), data, and copy — **not** chrome, spacing, typography, or background.

If you find yourself writing two separate "PackageDetailSheetShipper" and "PackageDetailSheetCarrier" composables with copy-pasted section layouts, extract a shared `PackageDetailSections` composable and have each role compose it with role-specific actions.

### 6. Don't fork — extend

When an existing `P*` *almost* fits but is missing a variant (e.g. `PButton` has primary / secondary but you need destructive):

1. **Extend** the existing primitive with the new variant in `:core:designsystem` (add the variant to the enum/sealed type, add tokens, add light + dark previews, add tests).
2. Update `android-spec/14-design-system.md` with the new variant.
3. Land that PR.
4. **Then** consume the new variant from the feature.

Do **not** copy `PButton` into the feature as a one-off bespoke button. Do **not** add a `customStyle: Boolean` flag that bypasses tokens.

### 7. Workflow before adding a UI file

```
About to add a composable
        │
        ▼
1. Search :core:designsystem for an existing P*
        │ found → use it (stop)
        ▼ not found
2. Search this feature's components/
        │ found → use / extend it (stop)
        ▼ not found
3. Search sibling features' components/ (cross-role surfaces)
        │ found → promote it to shared / :core:designsystem (separate PR), then use it
        ▼ not found
4. Will this be used by ≥ 2 features?
        │ yes → add the primitive to :core:designsystem first (with tests + previews + spec update)
        │ no  → add to features/<feature>/components/ as a reusable composable (rule 3)
        ▼
5. Build it ONLY from P* + Pasabayan* tokens (rule 2)
6. Add light + dark previews wrapped in PasabayanTheme
7. Stop after the slice for the user to commit
```

## Catching violations (review / self-review checklist)

Flag any of these in new or changed UI code:

- [ ] A new composable that duplicates the shape/role of an existing `P*` (a hand-rolled "card", "badge", "empty state", "row", "sheet header").
- [ ] A composable in `features/*/components/` that takes a `ViewModel`, performs I/O, or accepts a DTO/domain entity directly.
- [ ] A repeated UI block (≥ 2 uses or ≥ 30 lines) that was inlined instead of extracted.
- [ ] Two role-specific screens (shipper / carrier) with copy-pasted section layouts instead of a shared composable.
- [ ] A composable in `features/*/components/` that is actually used by **two or more** features — promote to `:core:designsystem`.
- [ ] A new variant added by a `Boolean` flag or `customColor: Color` parameter instead of being added to the `P*`'s variant enum in `:core:designsystem`.
- [ ] Missing `modifier: Modifier = Modifier` parameter on a reusable composable.
- [ ] Missing light + dark `@Preview` wrapped in `PasabayanTheme`.

## Anti-patterns

| Avoid | Prefer |
|---|---|
| `Card(modifier = Modifier.padding(12.dp).background(Color(0xFFF5F5F5)))` inline | `PCard { … }` (or extend `PCard` with the variant) |
| `MyFeatureButton(...)` that wraps `PButton` only to hardcode colors | Add the variant to `PButton` in `:core:designsystem` |
| `PackageDetailSheetShipper` + `PackageDetailSheetCarrier` with copied sections | `PackageDetailSections(...)` shared composable + role-specific action footers |
| `@Composable fun TripCard(viewModel: TripViewModel)` | `@Composable fun TripCard(state: TripCardState, onClick: () -> Unit, modifier: Modifier = Modifier)` |
| Inlining the same 40-line "user header row" in three screens | Extract `UserHeaderRow` to `features/<feature>/components/` (or `:core:designsystem` if cross-feature) |
| Adding `useDestructiveStyle: Boolean` to `PButton` | Add a `PButtonVariant.Destructive` enum case with proper tokens |

